WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专门为你制作了《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是“办公室女士”。

8
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.820
Oh, hi there.
噢，你好呀。

9
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:26.060
How are you?
你好吗？

10
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:27.220
I am well.
我很好。

11
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:29.000
How is New York City?
纽约市怎么样？

12
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.700
It is great.
棒极了。

13
00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.320
You know, I just love that we can do the podcast from two different cities.
你知道吗，我真喜欢我们能在两个不同的城市录制播客。

14
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.280
We're bi-coastal office ladies.
我们是跨越东西海岸的“办公室女士”。

15
00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:37.000
So cool.
太酷了。

16
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:40.800
I've got my sound engineer here, Casey, and we are ready to go.
我的音响工程师凯西在这儿，我们准备好开始了。

17
00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:45.700
I cannot believe we are on the second-to-last episode of Season 6.
真不敢相信我们已经录到第六季倒数第二集了。

18
00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:47.080
Me either.
我也是。

19
00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.480
It's crazy.
太疯狂了。

20
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:49.580
It's crazy.
太疯狂了。

21
00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:51.560
This is The Chump.
这一集叫《傻瓜》。

22
00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:57.660
It is Season 6, Episode 25, written by Erin Schur and directed by Randall Einhorn.
这是第六季第25集，由艾琳·舒尔编剧，兰德尔·艾因霍恩执导。

23
00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.640
Give us a summary, Jenna.
珍娜，给我们做个总结吧。

24
00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:00.740
Okay.
好的。

25
00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:02.040
Since you asked.
既然你问了。

26
00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:05.620
Here's your summary.
这是你的总结。

27
00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:14.560
Last week, Michael learned that Donna, the woman he's been seeing, is married and is cheating on her husband with Michael.
上周，迈克尔得知他正在交往的女人唐娜已婚，并且在和迈克尔偷情。

28
00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.920
But Michael does not call off the relationship.
但迈克尔并没有结束这段关系。

29
00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:22.620
And he receives a lot of flack from his employees for continuing his affair with Donna.
他因为继续与唐娜的婚外情而受到了员工们的严厉指责。

30
00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:32.740
Meanwhile, Pam and Jim struggle to stay awake at work after a late night with the baby, and Dwight and Angela are at odds over the validity of their co-parenting contract.
与此同时，帕姆和吉姆因为前一晚照顾孩子而熬夜，导致在工作中难以保持清醒；而德怀特和安吉拉则因为育儿协议的有效性而产生分歧。

31
00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:37.140
Oh, I have some good stuff about the Dwight-Angela co-parenting contract.
噢，关于德怀特和安吉拉的育儿协议，我有一些好料。

32
00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:39.300
I'll wait till we get to it.
等我们聊到那儿再说吧。

33
00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:43.640
I was hoping you would, lady, because I think there's stories there.
我就希望你这么说，女士，因为我觉得那里面有故事。

34
00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:44.620
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

35
00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:46.340
All right.
好的。

36
00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.040
Fast fact number one.
第一个速览事实。

37
00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:52.940
This was our 125th episode of The Office.
这是我们《办公室》的第125集。

38
00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:54.260
Wow.
哇。

39
00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:55.500
Yeah.
是啊。

40
00:01:55.980 --> 00:02:04.160
We shot this episode the week of March 19th, 2010, and it was viewed by 6.6 million people.
我们是在2010年3月19日那一周拍摄的这一集，有660万人收看了。

41
00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:06.580
That seems like a lot of folks.
那看起来人很多啊。

42
00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.100
It was a lot of folks.
确实很多人。

43
00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:12.320
We were second in the ratings right behind Grey's Anatomy.
我们的收视率排在第二，仅次于《实习医生格蕾》。

44
00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.440
They were a big competition at this time.
那时候它们可是强劲的竞争对手。

45
00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:18.980
I mean, it was a big deal if you were even holding your own with Grey's Anatomy.
我是说，能跟《实习医生格蕾》抗衡就已经很了不起了。

46
00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:19.760
I know.
我知道。

47
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.380
I mean, they were always number one.
我的意思是，它们总是排第一。

48
00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.900
Now, the reviews for this episode were pretty good.
这一集的评价相当不错。

49
00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:33.480
The AV Club gave it a B+, and it ranked as the 10th most well-liked episode by fans for Season 6 on Office Tally.
《影音俱乐部》给了它B+的评分，在“办公室计分板”网站上，它被粉丝评为第六季最受欢迎剧集的第10名。

50
00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:39.420
So, of all 26 episodes in Season 6, this was ranked 10th.
所以，在第六季全部26集中，这一集排在第10位。

51
00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.180
So, it was very well-liked.
所以，它非常受欢迎。

52
00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:42.420
I love a stat.
我喜欢数据。

53
00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.020
Oh, me too, lady.
噢，我也是，女士。

54
00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:51.620
Now, the fan-favorite moment that was most mentioned in the comments was, from this episode, there was a moment.
现在，评论区提到最多的粉丝最爱时刻，来自这一集里的某个片段。

55
00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.440
Oh, I'm going to guess, I'm Beyonce always.
噢，我来猜猜，我永远选碧昂丝。

56
00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.340
Oh, yes, that did get a lot of mentions.
噢，是的，那个确实被提到了很多次。

57
00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:59.120
That was very popular.
那个非常受欢迎。

58
00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:00.540
That's my favorite line.
那是我的最爱台词。

59
00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.280
That's a mug right there.
那绝对可以印在马克杯上。

60
00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:03.880
Yeah.
没错。

61
00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:15.060
No, the most popular moment was when Dwight and Angela are having sex in the warehouse, and it pans up to Pam and Jim listening from their sleeping spot.
不，最受欢迎的时刻是德怀特和安吉拉在仓库里发生关系时，镜头向上摇，拍到了吉姆和帕姆在他们睡觉的地方偷听。

62
00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:18.160
That's hilarious.
那太搞笑了。

63
00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:20.000
All right.
好吧。

64
00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:23.460
Fast fact number two is a location breakdown.
第二个速览事实是关于拍摄地点的解析。

65
00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:28.140
We got a fan question from Harmjen V in the Netherlands.
我们收到了来自荷兰的粉丝Harmjen V的提问。

66
00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:32.260
Where did you film the baseball game, and who were the players?
你们在哪里拍摄的棒球比赛，球员都是谁？

67
00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:34.080
Good question.
好问题。

68
00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:34.880
Yeah.
没错。

69
00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:43.280
I mean, a big portion of this episode takes place at a baseball field, with Michael and Andy watching Donna's husband, who is a high school baseball coach.
我是说，这一集很大一部分情节发生在棒球场，迈克尔和安迪在看唐娜的丈夫比赛，他是一位高中棒球教练。

70
00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:46.120
This was our first day of shooting.
这是我们拍摄的第一天。

71
00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:53.820
We filmed on location at College of the Canyons on Rockwell Canyon Road in Santa Clarita, California.
我们是在加利福尼亚州圣克拉里塔市罗克韦尔峡谷路的峡谷学院外景地拍摄的。

72
00:03:54.800 --> 00:04:01.740
And then our base camp, which is where they put all the trailers, and they put the food, and hair and makeup, everything.
然后是我们的基地营，就是他们放置所有拖车、餐饮、发型和化妆间以及所有东西的地方。

73
00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:02.580
Yes.
是的。

74
00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:05.760
That was in an adjacent parking lot.
就在隔壁的停车场。

75
00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:07.560
It was parking lot number eight.
那是八号停车场。

76
00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:15.000
So if you're a diehard fan, and you even want to tour our base camps, you can go to College of the Canyons parking lot eight.
所以如果你是铁杆粉丝，甚至想参观我们的基地营，你可以去峡谷学院的八号停车场。

77
00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:20.680
And that is where Steve Carell and Ed Helms had their lunch that day.
那天史蒂夫·卡瑞尔和艾德·赫尔姆斯就在那里吃的午餐。

78
00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:20.740
Okay.
好的。

79
00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:25.500
So everyone you see in these scenes are background performers.
所以你在这些场景中看到的每个人都是背景演员。

80
00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:29.360
Randy Cordray told me we had around 100 extras that day.
兰迪·科德雷告诉我那天我们大约有100名临时演员。

81
00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:30.980
For the baseball scenes?
是拍棒球戏吗？

82
00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:32.860
Yeah, for the baseball scenes.
对，拍棒球戏。

83
00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.360
He said that they went to Central Casting.
他说他们找的是中央选角公司。

84
00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:36.720
You know Central Casting.
你知道中央选角公司吧。

85
00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:38.880
That's the famous background casting agency.
那是很有名的背景演员选角机构。

86
00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:41.120
I was signed up with them when I first came to LA.
我刚到洛杉矶时就在他们那里注册过。

87
00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:42.200
I was signed up with them.
我也在他们那里注册过。

88
00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:44.020
You know my 90210 story.
你知道我那个《飞越比弗利》的故事。

89
00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.160
Oh, yes.
噢，知道。

90
00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:45.780
Yeah.
没错。

91
00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:46.380
Exactly.
正是如此。

92
00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:53.120
Well, Central Casting provided us with all of the spectators, and here is what we asked for.
嗯，中央选角公司为我们提供了所有的观众，以下是我们提出的要求。

93
00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:56.580
We wanted six people who could be grandparents.
我们需要六个看起来像祖父母的人。

94
00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:00.240
We wanted 18 adults to be parents.
我们需要18个成年人来扮演父母。

95
00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:10.100
And we needed 34 high school students, but all of the students had to be 18 years of age or older who looked younger, because then they could work adult hours.
我们还需要34名高中生，但所有学生必须年满18岁或以上，但看起来要年轻，因为这样他们才能按照成年人的工时工作。

96
00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:10.600
Right.
没错。

97
00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:17.320
But for the actual baseball scene, like the baseball players, we used a different company.
但对于实际的棒球戏，比如棒球运动员，我们用了另一家公司。

98
00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:22.100
I guess it's no longer in business, but it's called Smitty's Casting.
我想它现在已经倒闭了，但它叫史密提选角公司。

99
00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:23.880
Like Smitty with a Z.
就是那个带Z的史密提。

100
00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:25.860
Smitty's Casting.
史密提选角公司。

101
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.300
And they were really playing.
而且他们确实是在打球。

102
00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:32.240
Yeah, the players were really playing, and that's why we went to this casting place,
没错，演员们确实是在打球，所以我们才去了那个选角公司，

103
00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:40.100
because they're a specialty casting service that provides productions with sports-playing background performers.
因为他们是一家专门为影视制作提供会运动的背景演员的选角公司。

104
00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:48.500
So, we got enough people to fill two baseball teams, the Scranton Coalhawks and the Wolverines.
所以，我们找够了人组成了两支棒球队，斯克兰顿煤鹰队和狼獾队。

105
00:05:49.300 --> 00:06:02.080
Smitty's Casting sent us two male umpires, one male assistant coach, three male Wolverines coaches, 18 male Coalhawk players, and 18 male Wolverine players.
斯密蒂选角公司给我们派了两名男裁判、一名男助理教练、三名男狼獾队教练、18名男煤鹰队球员和18名男狼獾队球员。

106
00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:05.720
And then our wardrobe department provided the team uniforMs.
然后我们的服装部门提供了球队制服。

107
00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:08.020
I would have signed up for Smitty's.
我本来也会报名斯密蒂公司的。

108
00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:10.380
Maybe they would have taken me as a tennis player.
也许他们会录用我当个网球选手。

109
00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:13.100
Yes, exactly.
是的，没错。

110
00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:16.680
Can you play at, like, an almost professional level?
你能达到那种近乎职业的水平吗？

111
00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:20.380
Well, I, um, no, I can't.
嗯，我，呃，不，我不能。

112
00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:21.660
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

113
00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:23.200
I have a very good forehand.
我的正手击球非常棒。

114
00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:28.240
I think maybe you would just put that on your profile over at Central Casting.
我想你也许可以把这点写在中央选角公司的个人资料里。

115
00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:31.220
I'm sorry to say I'm not sure you qualify for Smitty's.
很遗憾，我不确定你是否符合斯密蒂公司的要求。

116
00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:32.140
Thank you for calling.
感谢您的来电。

117
00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:33.240
I don't make the Smitty's cut.
我没能通过斯密蒂公司的筛选。

118
00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:33.320
What?
什么？

119
00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:34.580
I'm so sorry.
非常抱歉。

120
00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:38.720
We are looking for professional level sports players.
我们正在寻找职业水平的运动员。

121
00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:39.500
Wow.
哇。

122
00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:42.220
Did you ever play on a college team or at the state level?
你曾经参加过大学校队或者州级比赛吗？

123
00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:45.180
No, Jenna, but I did play.
没有，珍娜，但我确实打过球。

124
00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:45.440
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

125
00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:46.000
I'm not Jenna.
我不是珍娜。

126
00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:48.080
I'm the woman on the phone at Smitty's.
我是斯密蒂公司接电话的那位女士。

127
00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:50.060
Oh, no, Barbara at Smitty's.
噢，不，是斯密蒂公司的芭芭拉。

128
00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:51.100
Here's the thing.
是这样的。

129
00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:55.560
I was once told by my high school coach that I have a lovely country club game.
我高中教练曾说我的球风很适合乡村俱乐部。

130
00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:56.140
So.
所以。

131
00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:58.200
Ma'am, I'm so sorry.
女士，非常抱歉。

132
00:06:58.420 --> 00:07:02.120
I'm going to have to just forward you over to Central Casting.
我只能把你转接到中央选角公司了。

133
00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:06.240
But congratulations on your terrific forehand.
不过还是要恭喜你拥有如此出色的正手击球。

134
00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:08.620
I hear some snark with Barbara.
我听出芭芭拉话里有讽刺意味。

135
00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:11.760
Well, you've kept Barbara on the phone for a very long time.
好吧，你已经霸占着芭芭拉的电话聊了很久了。

136
00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:16.100
She needs to move on to other calls that are actually going to produce a client.
她需要去处理其他能带来客户的电话了。

137
00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:16.680
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

138
00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:18.100
Barbara at Smitty's.
斯密蒂公司的芭芭拉。

139
00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:18.780
Listen.
听着。

140
00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:21.060
Listen, try being Barbara.
听着，试着当一下芭芭拉看看。

141
00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:21.940
Okay.
好吧。

142
00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:22.580
Not easy.
不容易。

143
00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:24.440
It's not easy to be Barbara.
当芭芭拉可不容易。

144
00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:25.860
Thank you for calling Smitty's.
感谢您致电斯密蒂公司。

145
00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:26.480
This is Barbara.
我是芭芭拉。

146
00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:30.240
Hey, so I would like to sign up for Smitty's.
嘿，我想报名加入斯密蒂公司。

147
00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:34.980
I play pool and also I can bowl very well.
我会打台球，而且保龄球也打得很好。

148
00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:36.620
Are you professional level?
你是职业水平吗？

149
00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:38.740
How do you define professional?
你是怎么定义职业的？

150
00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:39.620
Clicking.
挂断声。

151
00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:42.060
Look at the sass when you're Barbara.
看看你演芭芭拉时那股傲慢劲儿。

152
00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:42.960
Do you see what I'm saying?
你明白我的意思吗？

153
00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:44.460
Look what you have to deal with.
看看你得应付些什么。

154
00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:46.340
All right.
好吧。

155
00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:46.960
Okay.
行。

156
00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:48.660
Should we move on to fast fact number three?
我们要进入第三个速览事实了吗？

157
00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:49.700
Let's do it.
开始吧。

158
00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:52.320
I'm calling fast fact number three.
我来宣布第三个速览事实。

159
00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:54.700
Is there a guest star in the house?
现场有客串明星吗？

160
00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:56.620
Yes, there is.
是的，有。

161
00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:01.540
We have three new guest stars in this episode.
这一集我们有三位新客串明星。

162
00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:02.980
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

163
00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:06.760
They have all appeared on the TV show House.
他们都出演过电视剧《豪斯医生》。

164
00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:08.220
Oh.
哦。

165
00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:10.460
That's why there's a guest star in the house.
所以现场才会有“豪斯”明星。

166
00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:12.640
Oh, you're making a pun.
哦，你在玩双关语。

167
00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:14.160
I punned it.
我玩了个双关。

168
00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:15.100
You punned it.
你确实玩了。

169
00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:21.500
So Amy Peetz is back as Donna, but this fast fact refers to our never-before-seen guest stars.
艾米·皮茨回归饰演唐娜，但这个速览事实指的是我们从未见过的客串明星。

170
00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:26.460
For example, Bruno Oliver as our mediator, Mr. Barr.
比如饰演调解员巴尔先生的布鲁诺·奥利弗。

171
00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:35.060
He has been on Arrested Development, Mad Men, Modern Family, most recently in the movie Birds of Prey, and House.
他出演过《发展受阻》、《广告狂人》、《摩登家庭》，最近还参演了电影《猛禽小队》，以及《豪斯医生》。

172
00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:40.440
Bruno was so much fun, and he was just amazing.
布鲁诺太有趣了，他简直棒极了。

173
00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:42.780
Like, I loved all of our scenes.
我喜欢我们所有的对手戏。

174
00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:50.120
As an actor, I have to imagine that was such a fun guest star to come on the show and work with you and Rain in those scenes.
作为演员，我能想象到，作为客串明星来剧组和你们以及雷恩演对手戏一定很有趣。

175
00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:56.900
He was so good, too, as just the voice of reason between these two absolutely ridiculous people.
他演得也很好，简直是这两个极其荒谬的人之间理性的声音。

176
00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:58.920
He had some of my favorite lines.
他有一些我最喜欢的台词。

177
00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:05.040
So our other guest star is Donna's husband, Shane, who was played by Larkin Campbell.
我们的另一位客串明星是唐娜的丈夫肖恩，由拉金·坎贝尔饰演。

178
00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:13.660
Larkin has appeared in Passions, 24, Criminal Minds, Grey's Anatomy, our big competition, and also House.
拉金出演过《激情》、《24小时》、《犯罪心理》、《实习医生格蕾》——我们的劲敌，还有《豪斯医生》。

179
00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:22.520
Finally, our guest star Tina Huang, who played the reporter at the end, who confronts Michael about the exploding printers.
最后是客串明星蒂娜·黄，她在结尾饰演那个就爆炸打印机问题质问迈克尔的记者。

180
00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.540
She was a regular on the TV show Arrow.
她是电视剧《绿箭侠》的常驻演员。

181
00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:29.200
She also had a recurring role on Law & Order L.A.
她还在《法律与秩序：洛杉矶》中担任过常驻角色。

182
00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:32.400
That was a short-lived spinoff of the Law & Order series.
那是《法律与秩序》系列中一个短命的衍生剧。

183
00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:37.100
But I kid you not, she has also appeared on House.
但我没骗你，她也出演过《豪斯医生》。

184
00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:40.340
So there were guest stars in the House.
所以现场确实有“豪斯”明星。

185
00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:41.660
Nice.
不错。

186
00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:44.720
Well, that's all I got for Fast Facts.
好了，关于速览事实我就这些要说的。

187
00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:48.980
But I was very tickled when I was looking up all of the actors' resumes, and they had all been in-house.
但当我查阅所有演员的简历时，发现他们都演过《豪斯医生》，这让我感到非常开心。

188
00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:49.800
Different seasons.
不同的季数。

189
00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:55.720
Were you tickled by the fact that they had this crossover show or that you saw an opportunity to make a pun?
让你开心的是他们都有过这种交叉出演，还是你看到了玩双关语的机会？

190
00:09:56.180 --> 00:09:56.880
Both, lady.
两者都有，女士。

191
00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:03.600
Well, let's take a break, because when we come back, we're going to find a whole bunch of radon kits all over the office.
好了，我们休息一下，因为回来后，我们会在办公室各处发现一大堆氡气检测盒。

192
00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:05.100
Or are they ant traps?
还是说那是蚂蚁诱捕器？

193
00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:08.700
Or are they the little thing you turn upside down and it goes, moo?
又或者是那种倒过来会发出“哞”声的小玩意儿？

194
00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:11.340
Or are they none of the above?
还是说以上都不是？

195
00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:12.440
We'll be back.
我们马上回来。

196
00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:23.270
I think this might be Toby's happiest day.
我觉得这可能是托比最开心的一天。

197
00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:24.670
A hundred percent.
百分之百。

198
00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:26.690
Well, it starts as Toby's happiest day.
嗯，开始时确实是托比最开心的一天。

199
00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:28.470
Yes, absolutely.
是的，绝对是。

200
00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:29.830
It starts that way.
一开始是这样的。

201
00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:31.450
He's in the conference room.
他在会议室里。

202
00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:37.230
You guys, he is holding court about one of his favorite subjects, radon.
伙计们，他正在那儿高谈阔论他最喜欢的话题之一：氡气。

203
00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:50.600
One, he is explaining to everyone that he'll be placing radon kits all over the office, and he urges everyone, in particular Michael, and he's snapping at Michael,
首先，他向大家解释说他要在办公室各处放置氡气检测盒，并敦促大家，特别是迈克尔，而且他还在冲迈克尔发火，

204
00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:52.820
to please not throw them in the garbage.
请千万不要把它们扔进垃圾桶。

205
00:10:52.820 --> 00:11:03.660
At 13 seconds after Toby is snapping at Michael repeatedly, I want you to look at Steve's face as Michael, the way he glares at Toby.
在托比反复冲迈克尔发火的13秒后，我想让你们看看史蒂夫饰演的迈克尔的表情，他瞪着托比的样子。

206
00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:05.320
I went back and looked in the script.
我回去查了剧本。

207
00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:08.340
You know this was in the cold open shooting draft for Secretary's Day.
你们知道这是《秘书日》那集开场戏拍摄初稿里的内容。

208
00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:12.740
I had to know if this look to Toby was scripted.
我必须确认一下这个瞪托比的表情是不是剧本里写的。

209
00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:13.580
It was.
确实是。

210
00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:17.280
It said, Michael gives Toby an annoyed look.
剧本上写着：迈克尔给了托比一个恼火的眼神。

211
00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:20.760
And I want you to know, Jenna, we could not get through it.
而且我想让你知道，珍娜，我们当时根本演不下去。

212
00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:24.380
The first time Steve did it, we all erupted into laughter.
史蒂夫第一次做那个表情时，我们全都笑喷了。

213
00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:25.600
It's in the bloopers.
花絮里有这段。

214
00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:34.120
Well, we got a fan question, actually a fan mail flurry, asking, where is Pam during this cold open?
好吧，我们收到一个粉丝提问，其实是一连串粉丝来信，问：这段开场戏里帕姆去哪儿了？

215
00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:36.520
Was Jenna not available for filming?
是珍娜没空拍摄吗？

216
00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:37.560
Why am I not there?
为什么我不在那儿？

217
00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:40.340
When I watched this cold open, I actually thought the same thing.
当我看到这段开场戏时，我其实也想到了同样的问题。

218
00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:45.140
And then I remembered, like you said, this cold open was written for Secretary's Day.
然后我记起来了，就像你说的，这段开场戏是为《秘书日》那集写的。

219
00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:50.880
We actually shot it that week, and Pam was not back from her maternity leave yet.
我们确实是在那一周拍摄的，当时帕姆还没休完产假回来。

220
00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:54.460
She returns after the cold open, so that's why I'm not there.
她在开场戏之后才回归，所以这就是我不在那儿的原因。

221
00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:56.820
And that's why I did not get to see Steve's glare.
这也是为什么我没能看到史蒂夫那个瞪人的表情。

222
00:11:57.280 --> 00:11:58.420
Oh, yeah, that's right.
哦，对，没错。

223
00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:00.260
Pam is on maternity leave.
帕姆在休产假。

224
00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:02.040
Well, that's a great catch.
嗯，这真是个了不起的发现。

225
00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:09.680
Michael is going to have this talking head, and he is going to walk around his office and talk about all of the radon test kits.
迈克尔会有一个单人访谈，他会在办公室里走来走去，谈论所有的氡气检测盒。

226
00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:13.040
The first radon kit, he mistook for an ant trap.
第一个检测盒，他误以为是蚂蚁诱捕器。

227
00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:16.780
Then, of course, he thought it was the thing that you turn over that makes the cow noise.
然后，他当然又觉得那是那种翻过来会发出牛叫声的玩具。

228
00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:19.240
And he just keeps tossing him in the trash.
他就是不停地把它们扔进垃圾桶。

229
00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:21.900
The last one he tossed in the trash just out of spite.
最后一个他是纯粹出于恶意扔进垃圾桶的。

230
00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:28.720
Well, I asked Randy about these test kits, and it turns out these are not real radon test kits.
嗯，我问过兰迪关于这些检测盒的事，结果发现它们并不是真正的氡气检测盒。

231
00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:30.780
Fakie test kit alert.
假检测盒警报。

232
00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:33.360
Fakie radon test kit.
假氡气检测盒。

233
00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:34.100
Yeah.
没错。

234
00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:38.860
Randy said that the real ones at the time were actually pretty large and quite pricey.
兰迪说当时的真品其实挺大而且相当昂贵。

235
00:12:39.140 --> 00:12:44.660
And we were looking for something smaller that really did kind of look more like an ant trap.
我们当时在找一些更小、看起来确实更像蚂蚁诱捕器的东西。

236
00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:53.600
So, Phil Shea bought some inexpensive just electronic modules at Fry's Electronics for Toby to place around the office.
所以，菲尔·谢伊在弗莱电子买了一些便宜的电子模块，让托比放在办公室各处。

237
00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:59.580
And after we got them, we realized that they looked like the thing that goes moo.
等我们拿到手后，才发现它们看起来像那种会发出哞哞声的玩具。

238
00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:03.640
So, that line was added later after our purchase was made.
所以，那句台词是在我们买完东西后才加进去的。

239
00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:06.280
I was curious about that because it's so specific.
我对此很好奇，因为那句台词太具体了。

240
00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:07.920
And you know it's an instant memory.
而且你知道那是一种瞬间记忆。

241
00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:08.840
We all have.
我们都有过。

242
00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:10.500
We've all seen those things.
我们都见过那种东西。

243
00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:11.340
For sure.
确实。

244
00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:15.200
Angela, we got a piece of mail from Brent M.
安吉拉，我们收到了一封来自加拿大温哥华布伦特·M的邮件，他说，

245
00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:17.320
in Vancouver, Canada, who said,
我想知道你们这些女士是否了解关于氡气粉丝理论的任何信息。

246
00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:22.480
I was wondering if you ladies knew anything about the radon gas fan theory.
我不知道。

247
00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:23.900
I didn't.
我不知道。

248
00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:24.820
I don't.
我不知道。

249
00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:31.260
The radon gas theory basically suggests that everyone in the office is slowly getting poisoned by radon.
氡气理论基本上认为办公室里的每个人都在被氡气缓慢毒害。

250
00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:35.000
One of the side effects of radon poisoning is odd behavior,
氡气中毒的副作用之一就是行为怪异，

251
00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:38.820
which may explain the character's wacky behaviors in the later seasons.
这或许能解释该角色在后期剧集中的古怪行为。

252
00:13:38.820 --> 00:13:40.480
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

253
00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:48.500
So, you can go to the Reddit fan theories thread and you can read all about why the Scranton employees
所以，你可以去Reddit的粉丝理论帖，读读关于为什么斯克兰顿的员工们

254
00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:51.900
became so crazy in later seasons.
在后期剧集中变得如此疯狂的所有讨论。

255
00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:56.800
And the theory is that we are reacting to the radon gas and that Toby was right.
理论是说我们是因为氡气的影响才会有那样的反应，而且托比是对的。

256
00:13:57.440 --> 00:14:00.440
How many theories are there on this thread?
这个帖子里有多少种理论？

257
00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:06.900
Well, here was my thought about this theory is that it's kind of at odds with Toby being the Scranton strangler.
嗯，我对这个理论的想法是，它和“托比是斯克兰顿勒杀手”的设定有点冲突。

258
00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:12.940
I mean, wouldn't Toby want us to all die slowly from radon poisoning if he's the Scranton strangler?
我的意思是，如果托比是斯克兰顿勒杀手，他难道不希望我们都死于氡气中毒吗？

259
00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:16.640
I mean, it would be like he's slowly strangling us all to death.
我的意思是，这就像他在慢慢地把我们全都勒死一样。

260
00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:18.220
I mean, it's the slow play.
我是说，这是在放长线。

261
00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:19.160
Yeah.
没错。

262
00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:24.900
I mean, or maybe he's just, what, trying to throw us off with his theatrics?
我是说，或者他只是在干嘛，想用他的表演来迷惑我们？

263
00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:30.120
Like he's pretending to care about radon, but he really is just going to strangle us all later?
就像他假装关心氡气问题，但实际上只是打算以后把我们全都勒死？

264
00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:31.000
I don't know.
我不知道。

265
00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:34.780
So, it's making Toby really complex, if that's the case.
所以，如果真是这样的话，托比这个角色就变得非常复杂了。

266
00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:35.940
It's true.
确实。

267
00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:37.920
Very complex killer.
非常复杂的杀手。

268
00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:43.080
Well, Toby is going to say something that Michael cannot resiSt.
嗯，托比说了一句迈克尔无法抗拒的话。

269
00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:46.540
He says that radon gas is silent but deadly.
他说氡气是“无声但致命的”。

270
00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:48.060
Silent but deadly.
无声但致命。

271
00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:51.400
I mean, here comes Michael and fart noises.
我的意思是，迈克尔肯定会联想到屁声。

272
00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:52.280
It's going to happen.
这肯定会发生的。

273
00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:53.080
I know.
我知道。

274
00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:54.480
I mean, what did Toby expect?
我是说，托比到底指望什么呢？

275
00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:59.620
The group must be pretty bored by Toby because they're actually finding Michael's joke hilarious.
大家一定是被托比无聊坏了，因为他们竟然觉得迈克尔的笑话很好笑。

276
00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:02.100
Yes, until he goes too far.
是的，直到他做得太过火。

277
00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:03.760
Yeah.
没错。

278
00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:11.580
Yeah, he declares that if he had a gun with two bullets and he was stuck in a room with Hitler, bin Laden, and Toby, he would shoot Toby twice.
没错，他宣称如果他有一把装了两颗子弹的枪，又被关在一个房间里，面对希特勒、本·拉登和托比，他会朝托比开两枪。

279
00:15:12.020 --> 00:15:13.920
Then everyone's like, Michael.
然后大家都在喊，迈克尔。

280
00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:15.020
Michael, Michael.
迈克尔，迈克尔。

281
00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:15.460
No.
不。

282
00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:23.240
And then, of course, Dwight has to be Dwight and say that he could get all three with one bullet, and then he makes everyone line up to demonstrate.
然后，当然了，德怀特非要表现出德怀特的本色，说他可以用一颗子弹解决掉那三个人，接着他还让大家排好队来演示。

283
00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:25.580
And that's how the conference room meeting ends.
会议室的会议就是这样结束的。

284
00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:26.880
Yes, exactly.
是的，没错。

285
00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:30.400
Well, I have a little something about this cold open.
嗯，关于这个开场戏，我还有点小料。

286
00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:31.860
What's that?
是什么？

287
00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:34.520
You know it was in Secretary's Day.
你知道那是在“秘书节”那一集。

288
00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:36.500
We often moved our cold opens around.
我们经常会调整开场戏的位置。

289
00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:41.140
So, here is what was in the actual shooting draft for this episode.
所以，这是这一集实际拍摄剧本里的内容。

290
00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:43.680
The cold open featured Dwight,
开场戏的主角是德怀特，

291
00:15:43.780 --> 00:15:53.520
and he shares that he has one year's worth of provisions that can carry him through the chaotic first year of an apocalypse before cannibalism becomes accepted practice.
他分享说他存了一年的补给，足以支撑他度过末日混乱的第一年，直到吃人成为普遍做法。

292
00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:56.460
After that, he'll be on easy street.
在那之后，他就轻松了。

293
00:15:56.740 --> 00:16:03.420
But his provisions have a shelf life, so it's time to start eating and replacing everything that's about to expire.
但他的补给有保质期，所以是时候开始吃掉并更换那些快要过期的东西了。

294
00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:13.100
Then there's all this B-roll of Dwight eating smelly foods that have been stored for years, a jar of pickled okra, mackerel.
然后就是一堆德怀特吃那些存放多年、气味难闻的食物的空镜素材，一罐腌秋葵，鲭鱼。

295
00:16:13.340 --> 00:16:18.160
The bullpen is grossed out, and Jim, in particular, gives Dwight a lot of grief.
办公室里的其他人觉得很恶心，尤其是吉姆，他没少找德怀特的麻烦。

296
00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:19.660
Did we shoot that?
我们拍过那个吗？

297
00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:20.960
We did.
拍过。

298
00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:23.120
I have a memory of it.
我有印象。

299
00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:32.060
We did, and there is a really funny blooper on this Season 6 last DVD where you guys are all in the break room, and Dwight is eating gross stuff.
拍过，而且在第六季的最后一张DVD里有一个非常搞笑的NG花絮，你们都在休息室里，德怀特在吃那些恶心的东西。

300
00:16:32.060 --> 00:16:37.800
And he's going around and telling everyone how they would fare in this sort of zombie apocalypse.
他到处走，告诉每个人如果发生那种僵尸末日，他们会是什么下场。

301
00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:40.560
And Creed says, what would I do?
然后克里德问，我会怎么样？

302
00:16:40.820 --> 00:16:43.440
And Dwight said, your skull would be used as a bull.
德怀特说，你的头骨会被当成碗用。

303
00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:45.780
And Creed says, cool.
克里德说，酷。

304
00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:47.840
You guys couldn't get through it.
你们几个肯定受不了。

305
00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:50.620
Rain, John, they would disintegrate.
雷恩，约翰，它们会直接碎掉的。

306
00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:52.560
Every time, Creed was like, what would I do?
每次克里德都会问，我会怎么样？

307
00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:55.320
Every single time, Creed set his line.
每一次，克里德都坚持要说这句台词。

308
00:16:58.000 --> 00:16:59.260
Oh, that's amazing.
哦，太棒了。

309
00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:10.340
Well, this episode opens with Aaron and Pam working together to unpack some shopping bags filled with ice cream that is named after songs by the Eagles.
这一集开头，亚伦和帕姆一起拆开购物袋，里面装的是以老鹰乐队歌曲命名的冰淇淋。

310
00:17:11.020 --> 00:17:13.320
Yes, I loved the names of these ice creaMs.
没错，我超爱这些冰淇淋的名字。

311
00:17:13.520 --> 00:17:18.320
I kind of have a thing, Jenna, for ice cream flavors with fun names or crazy ice cream flavors.
珍娜，我对那些名字有趣或者口味疯狂的冰淇淋完全没有抵抗力。

312
00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:20.180
I just get so tickled by it.
我就是觉得特别好玩。

313
00:17:20.340 --> 00:17:21.100
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

314
00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:23.820
You are the marketing person's dream consumer.
你简直是市场营销人员梦寐以求的消费者。

315
00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:24.820
I know.
我知道。

316
00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:27.560
Oh, I will buy ice cream just if it has a fun name.
天哪，只要名字有趣，我就会买。

317
00:17:27.760 --> 00:17:34.860
So Aaron explains that the Eagles are doing a theme ice cream in honor of the Eagles turning 60, the band, the Eagles.
亚伦解释说，老鹰乐队为了庆祝乐队成立60周年，推出了主题冰淇淋。

318
00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:40.740
And the flavors are Desperado, Witchy, Wamanilla.
口味有《亡命之徒》、《巫婆》、《香草女郎》。

319
00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:44.180
And then later we find out Cake It to the Limit.
后来我们还发现了《把蛋糕吃到极限》口味。

320
00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:49.780
I had to know what were some of the craziest ice cream flavors out there.
我特别想知道市面上还有哪些疯狂的冰淇淋口味。

321
00:17:49.780 --> 00:17:54.740
And according to the website Taste of Home, here are just a few that caught my eye.
根据“家之味”网站的介绍，有几种口味特别吸引我。

322
00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:55.600
All right.
好吧。

323
00:17:55.940 --> 00:18:01.460
So Sam, Cassie, Casey, let me know if you guys would try any of these.
萨姆、卡西、凯西，你们告诉我，你们会尝试这些吗？

324
00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:07.440
First one, Kraft Macaroni and Cheese Ice Cream from Van Leeuwen Ice Cream.
第一个，Van Leeuwen冰淇淋出的卡夫通心粉奶酪冰淇淋。

325
00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:13.760
It has cream, milk, cane sugar, egg yolks, and, of course, tons of Kraft cheese powder.
它含有奶油、牛奶、蔗糖、蛋黄，当然还有大量的卡夫奶酪粉。

326
00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:16.800
You can find it in Brooklyn, New York, and also nationwide.
你可以在纽约布鲁克林买到，全国各地也有售。

327
00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:23.060
Lady Van Leeuwen's made a Grey Poupon ice cream that was just released recently, and I thought of you.
Van Leeuwen最近还出了一款灰博庞芥末冰淇淋，我当时就想到你了。

328
00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:24.700
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

329
00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:27.520
I would not eat that is the answer.
我的回答是，我绝对不会吃。

330
00:18:28.180 --> 00:18:30.100
That's a lactose intolerant nightmare.
那是乳糖不耐受者的噩梦。

331
00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:31.580
I would, yes.
我会吃，没错。

332
00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:33.860
You would eat the Kraft Mac and Cheese ice cream.
你会吃卡夫通心粉奶酪冰淇淋啊。

333
00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:34.680
Okay.
好吧。

334
00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:35.700
Moving on.
继续。

335
00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:40.140
Cheetos Flaming Hot Ice Cream from Marble Slab Creamery.
Marble Slab Creamery出的奇多火辣味冰淇淋。

336
00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:40.760
No.
不要。

337
00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:41.500
Listen.
听我说。

338
00:18:41.780 --> 00:18:41.830
No.
不要。

339
00:18:42.060 --> 00:18:42.820
It's got Flaming Hot...
它里面有火辣味……

340
00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:44.540
I won't eat a Flaming Hot Cheeto.
我连火辣奇多都不会吃。

341
00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:46.140
Why would I want it in my ice cream?
我为什么要把它放进冰淇淋里？

342
00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:50.160
It's got this sweet cream base with Flaming Hot Cheetos crushed.
它用的是甜奶油基底，里面碎着火辣奇多。

343
00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:50.740
Oh, my God.
天哪。

344
00:18:50.780 --> 00:18:53.360
You can get it also in a milkshake.
你还可以把它做成奶昔。

345
00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:54.400
Oh, God.
天哪。

346
00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:56.980
You can find it in Texas and Southeast states.
你可以在德克萨斯州和东南部各州买到。

347
00:18:57.180 --> 00:18:57.440
No.
不要。

348
00:18:57.680 --> 00:18:58.140
I mean...
我是说……

349
00:18:58.140 --> 00:19:00.100
I'm going to say yes, but I'm not proud of myself.
我会说我愿意尝试，但我一点也不以此为荣。

350
00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:01.200
You guys, I'm getting sick.
伙计们，我感觉要吐了。

351
00:19:01.420 --> 00:19:01.780
I'm getting...
我正准备……

352
00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:02.440
I don't feel well.
我感觉不太舒服。

353
00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:03.220
Sam is too...
萨姆太……

354
00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:04.800
Oh, well, then get ready for this one.
好吧，那做好心理准备迎接这个吧。

355
00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:13.080
Thanksgiving dinner from the ice cream store in Delaware is composed of egg yolk vanilla
特拉华州一家冰淇淋店的感恩节晚餐，是由蛋黄香草

356
00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:16.540
ice cream studded with tomatoes, potatoes, and green beans.
冰淇淋配上番茄、土豆和青豆制成的。

357
00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:21.040
This seasonal specialty is topped off with hot sauce and granulated sugar.
这款季节性特色美食最后还会淋上辣酱和砂糖。

358
00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:22.420
Thanksgiving dinner.
感恩节晚餐。

359
00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:23.580
What do you think?
你觉得怎么样？

360
00:19:23.860 --> 00:19:25.240
I mean, you only live once.
我是说，人生只有一次嘛。

361
00:19:25.820 --> 00:19:27.060
Oh, my God.
天哪。

362
00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:27.580
Casey.
凯西。

363
00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:30.360
I think it might just be an engineer thing.
我觉得这可能只是工程师的怪癖吧。

364
00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:31.200
Oh, my gosh.
天呐。

365
00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:31.460
Wait.
等等。

366
00:19:31.460 --> 00:19:32.400
I have two more.
我还有两个。

367
00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:32.980
Hold on.
等一下。

368
00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:33.500
I have a caveat.
我有个前提条件。

369
00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:35.020
Can I lay down after?
之后我能躺下吗？

370
00:19:35.380 --> 00:19:35.740
Yes.
可以。

371
00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:36.280
Sure.
当然。

372
00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:37.240
You would have to.
你肯定得躺下。

373
00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:38.540
If I can nap afterwards, yes.
如果之后能让我小睡一会儿，那就行。

374
00:19:38.540 --> 00:19:40.000
You can wear sweatpants and lay down.
你可以穿上运动裤躺下。

375
00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:40.920
Then yes.
那没问题。

376
00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:41.940
Okay.
好吧。

377
00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:43.980
Two last ones that caught my eye.
最后两个吸引我眼球的。

378
00:19:44.500 --> 00:19:47.900
Dill pickle from Dakota Drug Company in Stanley, North Dakota.
北达科他州斯坦利市达科他药业公司的酸黄瓜味。

379
00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:52.080
It's got a soft chestnut color that looks like caramel or peanut butter.
它呈现出一种柔和的栗色，看起来像焦糖或花生酱。

380
00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:55.580
This brine spike scoop is sure to surprise.
这一勺盐水味肯定会让人大吃一惊。

381
00:19:56.080 --> 00:19:58.360
I would try that just because it's one weird thing.
我会想尝尝，纯粹因为它太奇葩了。

382
00:19:58.480 --> 00:19:59.680
I don't think I would do that one.
我觉得我不会试那个。

383
00:19:59.780 --> 00:20:00.540
Oh, my gosh.
天呐。

384
00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:02.520
I'd be afraid it would ruin pickles for me.
我怕它会毁了我对酸黄瓜的印象。

385
00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:03.780
No, actually.
不，其实不会。

386
00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:09.300
And I know it's an audio podcast, so you can't see, but Jenna is contemplating hard.
我知道这是音频播客，你们看不见，但珍娜正在认真思考。

387
00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:13.440
No, I'm just, I'm not speaking because my stomach is turning.
不，我只是……我没说话是因为我胃里翻江倒海的。

388
00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:14.320
Or she's going to throw up.
或者她快要吐了。

389
00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:14.520
Never mind.
算了。

390
00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:15.060
Oh, my God.
天哪。

391
00:20:15.260 --> 00:20:15.460
Okay.
好吧。

392
00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:17.120
I'll quickly do the last one, Jenna.
我快速说最后一个，珍娜。

393
00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:21.120
Lobster from Ben and Bill's Chocolate Emporium.
本和比尔巧克力商场的龙虾味。

394
00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:22.020
What is happening?
这到底是怎么回事？

395
00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:25.180
You guys, just let the food be the food.
伙计们，让食物回归食物本身吧。

396
00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:28.740
It's delicious as it was made in its original form.
它原本的样子就已经很美味了。

397
00:20:28.840 --> 00:20:30.640
It doesn't need to be turned into a dessert.
没必要把它做成甜点。

398
00:20:31.060 --> 00:20:32.980
That one is in Falmouth, Massachusetts.
那家店在马萨诸塞州的法尔茅斯。

399
00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:35.440
Casey, how did you know that?
凯西，你怎么知道的？

400
00:20:35.560 --> 00:20:36.260
Have you had it?
你吃过吗？

401
00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:38.660
I've been to that place many times.
我去过那个地方很多次了。

402
00:20:38.720 --> 00:20:39.640
Have you eaten it?
你吃过吗？

403
00:20:39.640 --> 00:20:40.960
I have tried it.
我尝过。

404
00:20:41.180 --> 00:20:41.760
Oh, my God.
天哪。

405
00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:42.780
How is it?
味道怎么样？

406
00:20:43.460 --> 00:20:44.360
It's weird.
很奇怪。

407
00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:47.000
Does it taste like lobster?
吃起来像龙虾吗？

408
00:20:47.360 --> 00:20:49.000
It tastes lobstery, yeah.
确实有龙虾味，没错。

409
00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:51.020
Is it like buttery lobstery?
是那种黄油龙虾味吗？

410
00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:52.840
It's a little bit buttery.
带一点点黄油味。

411
00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:56.620
I would say more of the kind of crabby aspect comes through.
我觉得更多的是那种螃蟹的味道。

412
00:20:56.840 --> 00:20:58.300
Well, you want to know why?
你想知道为什么吗？

413
00:20:58.540 --> 00:20:59.640
Here are the ingredients.
配料表在这里。

414
00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:04.700
It's vanilla bean and butter-based lobster that has been cooked and chopped.
它是香草豆和黄油基底的龙虾，煮熟后切碎的。

415
00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:06.220
Do you get the bib?
你有围兜吗？

416
00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:07.920
I don't know.
我不知道。

417
00:21:07.920 --> 00:21:08.740
If so, then yes.
如果有的话，那就有。

418
00:21:08.940 --> 00:21:09.360
I don't know.
我不知道。

419
00:21:09.680 --> 00:21:14.260
Anyway, I took us on a tangent there because I find these ice cream flavors so fascinating.
总之，我刚才扯远了，因为我觉得这些冰淇淋口味太有意思了。

420
00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:16.300
Well, I'll tell you this.
好吧，我告诉你吧。

421
00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:18.360
Our ice creams were made up.
我们的冰淇淋是虚构的。

422
00:21:18.780 --> 00:21:20.200
The names were scripted.
名字也是编出来的。

423
00:21:20.780 --> 00:21:24.280
Randy Cordray said that Henry Sane built the graphics for the labels.
兰迪·科德雷说亨利·塞恩制作了标签的图形。

424
00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:27.560
And then, oh, no, I'm going to take us down a road.
然后，噢不，我又要扯远了。

425
00:21:28.460 --> 00:21:33.380
Phil Shea got the ice cream cartons made at a place called Earl Hayes Press.
菲尔·谢伊在一家叫厄尔·海耶斯印刷厂的地方定制了冰淇淋纸盒。

426
00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:40.460
And this is a very famous Hollywood business that mocks up printed items for TV shows and movies.
那是一家非常著名的好莱坞企业，专门为电视剧和电影制作印刷品模型。

427
00:21:40.680 --> 00:21:42.660
They've been around for a really long time.
他们已经存在很久了。

428
00:21:42.840 --> 00:21:43.720
We used them a lot.
我们经常用他们家的东西。

429
00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:45.660
Randy sent me their website.
兰迪把他们的网站发给了我。

430
00:21:46.260 --> 00:21:51.900
Lady, do you remember when I had to go to the old-timey prop house and I just wandered around for like an hour?
女士，你还记得我不得不去那家老式道具店，然后在里面逛了一个小时吗？

431
00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:53.680
You called me from there.
你当时从那儿给我打过电话。

432
00:21:53.820 --> 00:21:55.460
You were so tickled by it.
你当时觉得特别好玩。

433
00:21:55.580 --> 00:22:01.480
I think maybe in another life I was meant to be a prop master because I love it.
我觉得我上辈子可能是个道具师，因为我太喜欢那个了。

434
00:22:02.020 --> 00:22:03.560
But I looked at this website.
但我看了这个网站。

435
00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:07.380
It's all fakie labels for like made-up food brands.
上面全是虚构食品品牌的假标签。

436
00:22:07.560 --> 00:22:12.860
Like they'll make you a fakie cereal, a fakie yogurt, fakie mustard, like anything.
比如他们能帮你做假麦片、假酸奶、假芥末酱，什么都行。

437
00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:17.000
You know, so that you – because if you show a real label, you have to get clearance.
你知道的，因为如果你展示真实的标签，就必须获得授权。

438
00:22:17.300 --> 00:22:17.640
Yeah.
没错。

439
00:22:17.640 --> 00:22:24.640
