00:29:54.420 --> 00:29:56.380
And your teeth are red, Ange.
你的牙齿确实红了，安吉。

585
00:29:56.920 --> 00:29:58.040
They're really red.
真的很红。

586
00:29:58.160 --> 00:30:00.680
If you go to five minutes, seven seconds, you'll see.
如果你看到五分零七秒，你就会发现。

587
00:30:01.100 --> 00:30:07.540
Also, a fun little game, if you want to rewatch this episode, is you can see when my teeth are stained and when they aren't.
另外，如果你想重温这一集，有个有趣的小游戏，你可以观察我的牙齿什么时候染色了，什么时候没有。

588
00:30:07.540 --> 00:30:10.980
We go back and forth within the same scene.
我们在同一场戏里来回切换。

589
00:30:11.200 --> 00:30:12.280
I noticed that.
我注意到了。

590
00:30:12.640 --> 00:30:15.220
Well, we had a fan question from Cameron D.
我们收到了来自弗吉尼亚州里士满的卡梅伦·D的粉丝提问，

591
00:30:15.420 --> 00:30:20.420
in Richmond, Virginia, who said, what did you use for the beet-stained teeth?
他问，你们用什么东西让牙齿染上甜菜色的？

592
00:30:20.760 --> 00:30:22.200
Angela, was it gross?
安吉拉，那东西恶心吗？

593
00:30:22.580 --> 00:30:24.340
Were your teeth really stained?
你的牙齿真的被染色了吗？

594
00:30:24.340 --> 00:30:26.500
And Leanne H.
还有来自华盛顿州莱克史蒂文斯的莉安·H说，作为一名牙科保健员，

595
00:30:26.660 --> 00:30:30.180
from Lake Stevens, Washington, said, as a dental hygienist,
我很好奇安吉拉的甜菜色牙齿是怎么做出来的，因为颜色看起来很像牙科用来向患者展示刷牙遗漏牙菌斑的牙菌斑显示液。

596
00:30:30.380 --> 00:30:42.460
I was wondering how Angela's beet-stained teeth were achieved because the color looks similar to a dental disclosing solution used to show patients where they are missing plaque with their brushing.
我在想，你们是不是先把牙齿弄得很脏，然后用了这种溶液？

597
00:30:43.440 --> 00:30:47.680
I'm wondering, did you get your teeth really dirty and then use this solution?
不，莉安，我没那么做。

598
00:30:50.300 --> 00:30:51.900
No, Leanne, I didn't do that.
但我可以告诉你，负责我化妆的肯尼斯·保罗，我们对我的牙齿做了几次测试。

599
00:30:52.000 --> 00:30:56.700
But I will tell you, Kenneth Paul, who did my makeup, we did a few tests on my teeth.
他拿了一根棉签之类的东西。

600
00:30:56.780 --> 00:30:58.220
He had, like, a cotton swab.
他拿了一根棉签之类的东西。

601
00:30:58.220 --> 00:30:59.780
He also used, like, a little brush.
他还用了个小刷子之类的东西。

602
00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:02.440
And he had – it looked like a red food dye.
而且他还有——看起来像是红色的食用色素。

603
00:31:02.640 --> 00:31:04.940
It had no taste, so it didn't taste gross.
它没味道，所以吃起来不恶心。

604
00:31:04.940 --> 00:31:06.940
But it really made my teeth red.
但确实把我的牙齿染红了。

605
00:31:07.460 --> 00:31:09.580
And I thought we knocked this out of the park.
我觉得我们这次真是大获成功。

606
00:31:09.640 --> 00:31:11.060
I thought the teeth looked really red.
我觉得牙齿看起来真的很红。

607
00:31:11.060 --> 00:31:12.900
Kenneth Paul was happy with it.
肯尼斯·保罗对此很满意。

608
00:31:13.080 --> 00:31:17.820
Even when I walked to set, I would forget that my teeth were stained, and I would start talking to people.
甚至当我走到片场时，我都会忘了牙齿被染红了，然后开始跟人说话。

609
00:31:18.000 --> 00:31:19.460
And people would wince.
人们就会退缩。

610
00:31:19.660 --> 00:31:20.340
They'd go, ah!
他们会说，啊！

611
00:31:20.740 --> 00:31:28.080
And I actually became self-conscious while I had my teeth stained because everyone had such a reaction to it.
牙齿被染红的时候，我确实变得有点不自在，因为大家的反应太强烈了。

612
00:31:28.380 --> 00:31:32.020
But I remember they wanted my teeth even redder, Jenna.
但我记得他们想让我的牙齿更红，珍娜。

613
00:31:33.060 --> 00:31:36.140
Yeah, I guess this was a rather involved gag.
是啊，我想这算是个挺复杂的恶作剧。

614
00:31:36.660 --> 00:31:40.600
Randy Cordray said that, yes, in person, it was reading.
兰迪·科德雷说，是的，现场看的时候，效果是有的。

615
00:31:41.060 --> 00:31:42.340
If we were speaking to you.
如果我们是在跟你说话的话。

616
00:31:42.480 --> 00:31:47.660
But I guess, like, when they were looking at it in editing, it just didn't look red enough.
但我猜，他们在剪辑室看的时候，觉得红得不够明显。

617
00:31:47.840 --> 00:31:54.760
So they actually sent the shot of you showing your teeth to a visual effects company called Encore Video.
所以他们把那段你展示牙齿的镜头送到了一个叫Encore Video的视觉特效公司。

618
00:31:55.340 --> 00:31:58.980
And they added red to your teeth in poSt.
他们在后期给你的牙齿加了红色。

619
00:31:59.540 --> 00:32:01.200
Well, it really made me laugh.
好吧，这真的把我逗乐了。

620
00:32:01.360 --> 00:32:06.680
I had forgotten just how much of a visual gag it was until I rewatched it.
重看之前，我都忘了这视觉笑话的效果有多强。

621
00:32:06.740 --> 00:32:08.000
And I was like, oh, my gosh.
我当时心想，天哪。

622
00:32:08.520 --> 00:32:16.520
Well, lady, I got curious about the beet juice cleanse because I assumed this was just like a joke because of Dwight having a beet farm.
好吧，女士，我对甜菜汁排毒产生了好奇，因为我以为这只是因为德怀特有家甜菜农场而开的玩笑。

623
00:32:16.520 --> 00:32:19.420
But I guess it's actually a thing.
但看来这确实是种疗法。

624
00:32:20.180 --> 00:32:21.600
What kind of cleanse is it?
这是种什么样的排毒法？

625
00:32:21.920 --> 00:32:26.860
Well, according to JustBeatIt.com, B-E-E-T.
嗯，根据JustBeatIt.com，B-E-E-T。

626
00:32:27.260 --> 00:32:28.000
I love it.
我喜欢这个名字。

627
00:32:28.120 --> 00:32:35.540
Quote, an epic detoxifier that eliminates toxins from the liver, beets promote healthy liver function.
引用：一种史诗级的排毒剂，能消除肝脏毒素，甜菜能促进肝脏健康功能。

628
00:32:36.440 --> 00:32:47.760
And according to Tastylicious.com, beets have several essential health benefits that can help detoxify your body and give your organs and immune system a much-needed booSt.
根据Tastylicious.com，甜菜有几种重要的健康益处，可以帮助身体排毒，并为你的器官和免疫系统提供急需的助力。

629
00:32:48.460 --> 00:32:55.520
Aside from being healthy and packed full of vitamins, a beet juice cleanse has been known to help a range of conditions and ailments.
除了健康且富含维生素外，甜菜汁排毒法还被认为有助于改善多种疾病和不适。

630
00:32:55.800 --> 00:33:00.700
And it is the perfect food to prevent aging and to battle inflammation.
它是抗衰老和抗炎症的完美食物。

631
00:33:01.600 --> 00:33:04.220
Well, now I'm thinking we need to do a beet cleanse.
好吧，现在我在想我们是不是该做个甜菜排毒了。

632
00:33:04.860 --> 00:33:09.880
I mean, after drinking your beet juice vodka, lady, I mean, I don't know.
我是说，喝了你的甜菜汁伏特加之后，女士，我是说，我不知道。

633
00:33:10.420 --> 00:33:12.140
You really were not a fan.
你真的不太喜欢。

634
00:33:12.540 --> 00:33:14.960
It's just that it was so dry.
只是它太干了。

635
00:33:15.360 --> 00:33:16.780
It's very earthy.
味道非常土。

636
00:33:17.220 --> 00:33:21.180
Well, what I want to know is, is there a beet juice ice cream?
好吧，我想知道的是，有甜菜汁冰淇淋吗？

637
00:33:22.160 --> 00:33:23.680
Has anyone done that?
有人做过吗？

638
00:33:23.980 --> 00:33:24.700
I'm sure.
肯定有。

639
00:33:24.780 --> 00:33:25.300
Where's that flavor?
那种口味在哪儿呢？

640
00:33:25.980 --> 00:33:28.380
I'm positive there is one out there somewhere.
我敢肯定某个地方一定有。

641
00:33:28.680 --> 00:33:30.020
I would try that.
我会想尝尝。

642
00:33:30.520 --> 00:33:31.900
You would try beet ice cream.
你会想尝尝甜菜冰淇淋。

643
00:33:32.100 --> 00:33:35.140
Probably not the same health benefits as a beet juice cleanse.
可能没有甜菜汁排毒那样的健康益处。

644
00:33:35.320 --> 00:33:38.980
Incidentally, I could not really find any instructions for a beet juice cleanse.
顺便说一下，我没能找到任何关于甜菜汁排毒的具体说明。

645
00:33:38.980 --> 00:33:41.860
I could just find that beet juice is good for you.
我只能查到甜菜汁对你有好处。

646
00:33:42.200 --> 00:33:48.500
Well, now in the kitchen, Andy, Jim, Pam, and Phyllis are discussing how Michael just seems okay.
现在在厨房里，安迪、吉姆、帕姆和菲利斯正在讨论迈克尔看起来状态不错。

647
00:33:49.060 --> 00:33:50.580
You know, has he evolved?
你知道，他进化了吗？

648
00:33:50.740 --> 00:33:51.560
Has he matured?
他成熟了吗？

649
00:33:51.580 --> 00:33:52.380
He's not crying.
他没在哭。

650
00:33:52.640 --> 00:33:54.880
He's really handling this breakup well.
他处理这次分手的方式真的很成熟。

651
00:33:55.220 --> 00:33:55.980
I know.
我知道。

652
00:33:56.520 --> 00:33:57.780
And Jim's like, so what?
然后吉姆就说，那又怎样？

653
00:33:57.840 --> 00:33:59.020
He just matured overnight?
他是一夜之间就成熟了吗？

654
00:33:59.020 --> 00:34:00.960
And Andy's like, that's what happened in big.
安迪就说，这就是大人们发生的事。

655
00:34:02.680 --> 00:34:03.080
Yeah.
是啊。

656
00:34:04.580 --> 00:34:08.160
Well, Pam and Jim are going to make an announcement.
嗯，帕姆和吉姆要宣布一件事。

657
00:34:08.880 --> 00:34:10.800
This was so well done.
这一段拍得真好。

658
00:34:11.020 --> 00:34:16.880
I thought you and John crushed this moment because you look so weary.
我觉得你和约翰把这一刻演绝了，因为你们看起来那么疲惫。

659
00:34:16.880 --> 00:34:23.540
And inviting Michael to come to your house and play with your baby and you order food to go from Hooters.
还要邀请迈克尔去你家玩孩子，然后你还点了猫头鹰餐厅的外卖。

660
00:34:23.880 --> 00:34:24.320
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

661
00:34:24.760 --> 00:34:27.920
You look so pained as you're saying all of it, Jenna.
珍娜，你说这些话的时候看起来好痛苦。

662
00:34:28.200 --> 00:34:29.520
It just cracked me up.
这真的把我逗乐了。

663
00:34:30.520 --> 00:34:39.160
It reminded me of the scene where Pam is trying to get Michael to talk to her so she tells him that she needs to discuss her sex life with him.
这让我想起了帕姆为了让迈克尔跟她说话，告诉他自己需要跟他讨论性生活的那一幕。

664
00:34:39.400 --> 00:34:39.600
Yeah.
是啊。

665
00:34:39.920 --> 00:34:41.500
They really know Michael well.
他们真的很了解迈克尔。

666
00:34:41.800 --> 00:34:42.340
They do.
确实。

667
00:34:42.760 --> 00:34:47.240
Even after all of these promises, Michael is going to take a rain check.
即使做了这么多承诺，迈克尔还是打算改天再说。

668
00:34:47.780 --> 00:34:51.080
And that is when Pam says, are you still seeing Donna?
就在那时，帕姆问，你还在和唐娜见面吗？

669
00:34:51.620 --> 00:34:54.240
She yells it across the bullpen.
她隔着办公区大喊出来。

670
00:34:54.240 --> 00:34:59.260
I wrote down the time code five minutes and 56 seconds into the episode.
我记下了时间码，在剧集的5分56秒处。

671
00:34:59.520 --> 00:35:01.060
I couldn't believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

672
00:35:01.220 --> 00:35:03.420
Like, I was like, wow, Pam.
当时我就想，哇，帕姆。

673
00:35:03.820 --> 00:35:06.160
I have something to say about this scene.
关于这一幕我有些话要说。

674
00:35:06.360 --> 00:35:10.980
One of the things that Pam offers to do with Michael is play rock band.
帕姆提议和迈克尔一起做的事情之一就是玩《摇滚乐队》游戏。

675
00:35:11.280 --> 00:35:14.920
She says they'll play Billy Joel songs on rock band.
她说他们要在《摇滚乐队》里唱比利·乔尔的歌。

676
00:35:15.140 --> 00:35:18.620
Now, first of all, Billy Joel songs were never on rock band.
首先，比利·乔尔的歌从来没在《摇滚乐队》里出现过。

677
00:35:18.840 --> 00:35:21.820
He hadn't given permission to use his songs.
他当时还没授权使用他的歌曲。

678
00:35:21.860 --> 00:35:23.380
So this is something that we made up.
所以这是我们编出来的。

679
00:35:23.380 --> 00:35:28.780
And the reason that I would know this is because I got really, really into rock band for a while.
之所以我知道这一点，是因为我有一段时间特别沉迷《摇滚乐队》。

680
00:35:28.960 --> 00:35:33.280
And I don't know if you remember, but I used to come to set and I used to talk about it.
我不确定你还记不记得，但我以前常去片场谈论这个。

681
00:35:33.620 --> 00:35:38.780
And I even had some folks over to my house for a barbecue to play rock band.
我甚至还邀请了一些人到我家烧烤，一起玩《摇滚乐队》。

682
00:35:39.280 --> 00:35:44.260
And I kind of like to imagine that maybe that's how rock band made it into this episode.
我有点想当然地认为，也许这就是《摇滚乐队》出现在这一集里的原因。

683
00:35:44.980 --> 00:35:47.680
I do remember you having a thing for rock band.
我确实记得你当时对《摇滚乐队》很着迷。

684
00:35:48.020 --> 00:35:49.660
I was not part of it.
我没参与其中。

685
00:35:50.140 --> 00:35:50.520
I didn't.
我没玩。

686
00:35:50.520 --> 00:35:55.080
Oh, lady, I know that you couldn't because it was a late night thing and you had a child.
噢，亲爱的，我知道你没法玩，因为那是深夜活动，而且你当时有孩子。

687
00:35:55.300 --> 00:35:56.100
And I was still...
而我当时还是……

688
00:35:56.940 --> 00:35:57.060
I had a baby.
我当时有个宝宝。

689
00:35:57.620 --> 00:36:01.320
You were my friend who was still playing video games late at night.
你是我那个还在深夜玩电子游戏的朋友。

690
00:36:01.540 --> 00:36:01.960
Exactly.
没错。

691
00:36:02.040 --> 00:36:05.880
I'm sure this was me at my most annoying for you as a new mother.
我敢肯定，对于身为新妈妈的你来说，那时的我一定烦人透了。

692
00:36:06.780 --> 00:36:08.060
But you did love it.
但你确实很喜欢它。

693
00:36:08.200 --> 00:36:10.100
It had to have made its way in because of you.
它一定是因为你才被写进剧本里的。

694
00:36:10.260 --> 00:36:11.580
I'm going to co-sign on that.
我同意这个说法。

695
00:36:11.800 --> 00:36:12.100
Okay.
好的。

696
00:36:12.100 --> 00:36:12.680
Thank you.
谢谢。

697
00:36:13.300 --> 00:36:17.020
Well, now Michael is going to have his orange lips talking head.
好了，现在迈克尔要进行他的橙色嘴唇采访了。

698
00:36:17.660 --> 00:36:18.020
Yeah.
是啊。

699
00:36:18.460 --> 00:36:19.540
What was that?
那是什么情况？

700
00:36:19.680 --> 00:36:20.820
I noticed it too.
我也注意到了。

701
00:36:21.280 --> 00:36:21.700
Yeah.
是啊。

702
00:36:22.080 --> 00:36:24.800
He has this talking head where he says he likes Donna.
他有个访谈镜头，说他喜欢唐娜。

703
00:36:25.100 --> 00:36:28.180
And if it's wrong to keep seeing her, he doesn't care.
如果继续和她交往是错的，他也不在乎。

704
00:36:28.800 --> 00:36:30.500
And he has orange lips.
而且他的嘴唇是橘色的。

705
00:36:30.640 --> 00:36:34.980
And the message boards after this episode had all these comments.
这集播出后的留言板上全是这种评论。

706
00:36:34.980 --> 00:36:37.540
Why did Michael have orange lips?
为什么迈克尔的嘴唇是橘色的？

707
00:36:37.740 --> 00:36:39.220
Were there any fan theories?
有什么粉丝理论吗？

708
00:36:39.360 --> 00:36:40.300
Because I have one.
因为我有一个。

709
00:36:41.140 --> 00:36:43.040
There was a fan theory.
确实有个粉丝理论。

710
00:36:43.500 --> 00:36:46.060
First of all, there was no mention of it in the script.
首先，剧本里根本没提这事。

711
00:36:46.320 --> 00:36:52.800
But the one fan theory is that his lips are stained from kissing Donna, who wears red lipstick.
但其中一个粉丝理论是，他的嘴唇是被唐娜亲红的，因为唐娜涂了红唇膏。

712
00:36:53.660 --> 00:36:53.940
Okay.
好吧。

713
00:36:54.260 --> 00:36:55.440
Here was my theory.
这是我的理论。

714
00:36:55.900 --> 00:36:56.140
Okay.
好。

715
00:36:57.020 --> 00:37:00.120
So, later in the episode, he comes in with all of these oranges.
这集后面，他带了一大堆橘子进来。

716
00:37:00.660 --> 00:37:01.180
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

717
00:37:01.360 --> 00:37:05.000
And I wondered if maybe we shot out of order and Steve ate a bunch of oranges.
我在想是不是因为拍摄顺序不对，史蒂夫吃了一堆橘子。

718
00:37:06.220 --> 00:37:07.980
Oh, my gosh, lady.
天哪，女士。

719
00:37:08.360 --> 00:37:09.380
I'm going to go with you.
我支持你的想法。

720
00:37:09.940 --> 00:37:11.160
I mean, I don't know.
我是说，我也不确定。

721
00:37:11.220 --> 00:37:15.020
Well, how many oranges do you have to eat for your lips to take on some color?
话说，得吃多少橘子嘴唇才会变色啊？

722
00:37:15.180 --> 00:37:19.340
But that's all I could think of was, well, we really did eat a bunch of oranges.
但我当时能想到的就是，我们确实吃了一堆橘子。

723
00:37:19.660 --> 00:37:20.180
We did.
我们确实吃了。

724
00:37:20.520 --> 00:37:21.520
You might be right.
你说得对。

725
00:37:22.040 --> 00:37:26.020
Well, the bullpen is really going to confront Michael on having this affair.
办公室职员们真的要找迈克尔对质这段婚外情了。

726
00:37:26.140 --> 00:37:32.260
