01:00:04.420 --> 01:00:06.720
We see her sitting in her car waiting for him.
我们看到她坐在车里等他。

1163
01:00:07.060 --> 01:00:08.740
Do you know what that hotel was, Ange?
安吉，你知道那是哪家酒店吗？

1164
01:00:09.000 --> 01:00:10.800
No, but it had a bright orange door.
不知道，但它有一扇亮橙色的门。

1165
01:00:11.400 --> 01:00:11.900
Yeah.
没错。

1166
01:00:12.460 --> 01:00:15.560
Do you know the Tangerine Hotel in Burbank?
你知道伯班克的橘子酒店吗？

1167
01:00:16.460 --> 01:00:17.380
Oh, is it that one?
哦，是那家吗？

1168
01:00:17.380 --> 01:00:19.280
You would know it if you drove by it.
如果你开车经过，肯定会认出来的。

1169
01:00:19.380 --> 01:00:20.020
Yes, yes, I do.
是的，我知道。

1170
01:00:20.280 --> 01:00:21.940
That was the hotel we used.
那就是我们用的酒店。

1171
01:00:22.240 --> 01:00:22.700
Oh.
哦。

1172
01:00:22.900 --> 01:00:24.840
And it has the bright orange door.
而且它确实有那扇亮橙色的门。

1173
01:00:25.120 --> 01:00:25.420
Yeah.
没错。

1174
01:00:25.960 --> 01:00:26.260
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1175
01:00:26.720 --> 01:00:27.720
I couldn't believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

1176
01:00:27.780 --> 01:00:28.500
Randy told me that.
是兰迪告诉我的。

1177
01:00:28.620 --> 01:00:29.440
I was like, yes!
我当时就想，太棒了！

1178
01:00:29.660 --> 01:00:30.000
Oh, my gosh!
天哪！

1179
01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:32.500
I knew I knew it, but I didn't know how I knew it.
我知道我认得它，但我不知道是怎么认出来的。

1180
01:00:32.800 --> 01:00:33.180
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1181
01:00:33.380 --> 01:00:34.140
It's still there.
它还在那儿呢。

1182
01:00:34.220 --> 01:00:34.720
Famous hotel.
很有名的酒店。

1183
01:00:35.480 --> 01:00:41.320
Michael's going to have a talking head where he tells us that he feels good.
迈克尔会有一个采访镜头，告诉我们他感觉很好。

1184
01:00:41.320 --> 01:00:45.000
He broke up with Donna, and he knows he made the right decision.
他和唐娜分手了，他知道自己做了正确的决定。

1185
01:00:45.820 --> 01:00:48.520
But then, of course, he broke my heart a little bit.
但当然，他还是让我有点心碎。

1186
01:00:48.520 --> 01:00:56.440
He had to choose between happiness or living with himself, and he chose living with himself, which means he had to give up his happiness.
他必须在幸福和问心无愧之间做出选择，他选择了问心无愧，这意味着他不得不放弃自己的幸福。

1187
01:00:57.060 --> 01:00:57.320
Yeah.
没错。

1188
01:00:58.080 --> 01:01:00.960
And now he's going to be, you know, lonely again.
现在他又得，你知道，重新变得孤独了。

1189
01:01:01.460 --> 01:01:01.680
Yeah.
没错。

1190
01:01:02.160 --> 01:01:03.460
But he does the right thing.
但他做了正确的事。

1191
01:01:03.700 --> 01:01:09.300
He does the right thing, and he's going to go back to the office and grab his ice cream.
他做了正确的事，他打算回到办公室去拿他的冰淇淋。

1192
01:01:09.800 --> 01:01:10.120
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1193
01:01:10.620 --> 01:01:14.120
Pam and Jim don't know if they can make it through the rest of the day.
帕姆和吉姆不知道他们能不能撑过这一天剩下的时间。

1194
01:01:14.360 --> 01:01:15.620
They're really struggling.
他们真的很煎熬。

1195
01:01:16.320 --> 01:01:21.160
And Daryl tells them where they can go to sleep in the warehouse.
达里尔告诉他们仓库里有个地方可以去睡觉。

1196
01:01:21.500 --> 01:01:23.000
There's this little secret spot.
那是一个小小的秘密基地。

1197
01:01:23.320 --> 01:01:27.520
Daryl loves it so much, sometimes he thinks about it when he's at home trying to go to sleep.
达里尔太喜欢那个地方了，有时他在家准备睡觉时都会想到它。

1198
01:01:27.520 --> 01:01:32.780
I don't know if this was on the bloopers, Angela, but we could not get through this scene with Craig.
安吉拉，我不知道这有没有被收进花絮里，但我们拍这场戏时总是忍不住笑场。

1199
01:01:33.340 --> 01:01:44.500
When Craig was, like, wistfully talking about the sleeping spot, like, his voice, he's like, sometimes I think about it, so warm.
当克雷格用那种向往的语气谈论那个睡觉的地方时，他的声音，他说，有时我会想到它，那么温暖。

1200
01:01:44.720 --> 01:01:45.960
Like, we would laugh.
我们当时真的笑个不停。

1201
01:01:46.120 --> 01:01:47.240
It was so funny.
那真的太搞笑了。

1202
01:01:47.560 --> 01:01:52.520
It's not in the bloopers, but there is a really funny Daryl talking head in the bloopers from this episode.
虽然正片花絮里没有，但这一集的拍摄花絮里有一段达里尔的采访片段，真的特别好笑。

1203
01:01:52.520 --> 01:02:00.440
It was deleted, so it's not in the episode, but Daryl shares that he used to cheat, but then he watched the movie Love Actually, and that really set him straight.
那段被删减了，所以正片里没有，但达里尔在里面分享说他以前经常作弊，后来他看了电影《真爱至上》，那部电影让他彻底改邪归正了。

1204
01:02:00.700 --> 01:02:01.600
It really got to him.
那部电影对他触动很大。

1205
01:02:02.060 --> 01:02:05.080
And he kept laughing through it, and it's really funny.
他一直在笑场，真的特别好笑。

1206
01:02:05.420 --> 01:02:14.480
Well, I guess Angela has picked one of her moments, one of her five moments with Dwight, and they are going to rendezvous back in their meeting place in the warehouse.
我想安吉拉选了她和德怀特那五个高光时刻里的一个，他们打算在仓库里的老地方幽会。

1207
01:02:15.040 --> 01:02:16.760
Dwight says, Angela, are you warmed up?
德怀特问：“安吉拉，你热身了吗？”

1208
01:02:16.860 --> 01:02:17.600
She says, no.
她说：“没有。”

1209
01:02:17.760 --> 01:02:20.320
And he goes, why is that always my responsibility?
然后他说：“为什么这种事总得我来负责？”

1210
01:02:21.460 --> 01:02:25.920
And then they go in, and they shut the door, and she goes, what have you done to yourself?
接着他们走进去关上门，她说：“你把自己搞成什么样了？”

1211
01:02:26.380 --> 01:02:28.180
You start hearing some noises.
你开始听到一些动静。

1212
01:02:28.180 --> 01:02:29.400
He's like, no kissing.
他说：“不许接吻。”

1213
01:02:29.400 --> 01:02:33.320
This is a really awkward thing to overhear, and guess who's overhearing it?
无意中听到这些真的很尴尬，你猜是谁听到了？

1214
01:02:33.800 --> 01:02:34.060
Yeah.
没错。

1215
01:02:34.580 --> 01:02:35.300
Jim and Pam.
吉姆和帕姆。

1216
01:02:36.000 --> 01:02:37.180
Poor Jim and Pam.
可怜的吉姆和帕姆。

1217
01:02:37.340 --> 01:02:46.860
All they wanted to do was go to this special little sleeping nook that Daryl told them about in the warehouse, and now they're overhearing Dwight and Angela.
他们本来只想去达里尔告诉他们的那个仓库里的秘密小睡角，结果却撞见了德怀特和安吉拉。

1218
01:02:46.860 --> 01:02:52.160
So I have to tell you, getting to our sleeping spot was actually very complicated.
我得告诉你们，去到我们那个睡觉的地方其实非常复杂。

1219
01:02:52.520 --> 01:02:54.160
Yeah, you guys are up really high.
是啊，你们当时爬得特别高。

1220
01:02:54.420 --> 01:02:54.840
Yes.
没错。

1221
01:02:54.860 --> 01:02:57.960
We are actually up on a shelf in the warehouse.
我们其实是在仓库的一个货架上。

1222
01:02:57.960 --> 01:03:00.300
It's a special thing that they built.
那是他们专门搭建的一个地方。

1223
01:03:00.840 --> 01:03:08.280
Randy reminded me that we actually had to practice getting up there using a scissor lift.
兰迪提醒我，我们当时还得练习怎么用剪叉式升降机爬上去。

1224
01:03:08.280 --> 01:03:09.000
Wow.
哇。

1225
01:03:09.300 --> 01:03:17.020
And it involved a whole rehearsal the week prior with a Universal Studios safety officer named Ian Bass Gillespie.
而且前一周还专门为此进行了一次彩排，有一位名叫伊恩·巴斯·吉莱斯皮的环球影城安全员在场。

1226
01:03:17.540 --> 01:03:23.960
This person was in attendance to sign off on our use of the scissor lift, and it was a big deal.
那个人在场是为了批准我们使用升降机，这可是件大事。

1227
01:03:24.160 --> 01:03:32.480
But we made it up there, and we're laying truly up on this high shelf in this little nook.
但我们最终还是上去了，我们就那样躺在那个高高的货架上的小角落里。

1228
01:03:32.480 --> 01:03:36.500
And I will tell you right now, it was so comfy cozy.
我现在就可以告诉你，那里真的非常舒服惬意。

1229
01:03:36.960 --> 01:03:40.540
It was everything that Daryl advertised it to be.
它完全符合达里尔所描述的样子。

1230
01:03:40.840 --> 01:03:47.060
And it was a dream to just sort of get to kind of nap for part of my workday.
能在工作时间小睡一会儿简直就像做梦一样。

1231
01:03:47.860 --> 01:03:51.780
All I could think about when I saw you guys up there was, what if you have to pee?
我看到你们在那上面时，脑子里想的全是：要是你们想上厕所怎么办？

1232
01:03:54.240 --> 01:03:55.760
That's what I always think.
我总是会想这个问题。

1233
01:03:56.220 --> 01:03:57.680
Like, could you imagine?
你能想象吗？

1234
01:03:57.860 --> 01:04:01.120
That is why I never want to sleep on the top bunk of a bunk bed.
这就是我为什么从来不想睡双层床的上铺。

1235
01:04:01.120 --> 01:04:01.960
I know!
我懂！

1236
01:04:02.400 --> 01:04:05.300
Well, we had a fan question from Michelle S.
好吧，我们收到一个来自澳大利亚墨尔本的米歇尔·S的粉丝提问。

1237
01:04:05.460 --> 01:04:09.320
in Melbourne, Australia that I thought was very wise.
我觉得这个问题问得很有水平。

1238
01:04:09.840 --> 01:04:10.900
Michelle said,
米歇尔说：

1239
01:04:11.180 --> 01:04:17.340
The spot where the warehouse guys take their naps is right above Dwight and Angela's sex spot.
“仓库员工午睡的地方就在德怀特和安吉拉偷情地点的正上方。”

1240
01:04:17.660 --> 01:04:21.940
Does this mean that the warehouse guys know about Dwight and Angela's affair?
“这是否意味着仓库员工其实知道德怀特和安吉拉的私情？”

1241
01:04:22.260 --> 01:04:22.640
Ah!
啊！

1242
01:04:23.120 --> 01:04:25.720
I mean, they've been there the whole time.
我是说，他们一直都在那里。

1243
01:04:25.960 --> 01:04:26.340
Ah!
啊！

1244
01:04:26.860 --> 01:04:29.480
I think the warehouse guys do know about your affair.
我觉得仓库员工确实知道你们的私情。

1245
01:04:29.740 --> 01:04:30.740
Oh, for sure.
噢，那肯定的。

1246
01:04:31.120 --> 01:04:34.980
I don't think you guys are hiding it from them at all.
我觉得你们根本就没瞒住他们。

1247
01:04:35.280 --> 01:04:38.420
Clearly, we haven't been hiding it very well from anyone.
显然，我们对谁都没瞒好。

1248
01:04:38.920 --> 01:04:39.460
Exactly.
确实。

1249
01:04:41.280 --> 01:04:46.620
Well, the episode is going to end with Michael exiting the building, and he's approached by a news team.
这一集结尾是迈克尔走出大楼，然后被一个新闻团队拦住了。

1250
01:04:46.960 --> 01:04:48.080
The reporter says,
记者说：

1251
01:04:48.200 --> 01:04:50.680
Michael Scott, do you want to make a comment on the rumors?
迈克尔·斯科特，你对这些传闻有什么想说的吗？

1252
01:04:51.380 --> 01:04:52.420
Michael sighs.
迈克尔叹了口气。

1253
01:04:52.740 --> 01:04:53.200
He's like,
他说，

1254
01:04:53.200 --> 01:04:59.180
I have done some very bad things, things of which I am not proud.
我做了一些非常糟糕的事情，一些让我感到羞愧的事情。

1255
01:04:59.260 --> 01:05:09.040
I would like to publicly apologize to the coach and the players, and I vow to never listen to my bodily instincts ever again.
我想公开向教练和球员们道歉，我发誓再也不会听从我身体的本能了。

1256
01:05:09.040 --> 01:05:11.980
The reporter is confused.
记者感到困惑。

1257
01:05:12.060 --> 01:05:12.620
The reporter is confused.
记者感到困惑。

1258
01:05:12.620 --> 01:05:13.640
She says,
她说，

1259
01:05:14.300 --> 01:05:17.260
I'm talking about the saber printers that catch on fire.
我说的是那些会着火的赛博打印机。

1260
01:05:17.900 --> 01:05:18.840
And Michael's like,
迈克尔说，

1261
01:05:18.940 --> 01:05:20.400
Oh, okay, I was talking about,
哦，好的，我刚才说的是，

1262
01:05:20.540 --> 01:05:21.200
Wait, wait, what?
等等，等等，什么？

1263
01:05:21.780 --> 01:05:22.340
Yeah.
是啊。

1264
01:05:22.340 --> 01:05:28.080
So, Randy told me that this was like a standards and practices issue.
所以，兰迪告诉我这就像是一个标准和规范的问题。

1265
01:05:28.340 --> 01:05:28.900
This scene.
这一幕。

1266
01:05:29.120 --> 01:05:29.660
Why?
为什么？

1267
01:05:30.040 --> 01:05:31.460
That's what I asked.
我当时就是这么问的。

1268
01:05:31.640 --> 01:05:36.700
He said that they wanted us to create a fictitious news channel.
他说他们希望我们虚构一个新闻频道。

1269
01:05:37.480 --> 01:05:41.940
They didn't want us to use the real NBC affiliate, which is WBRE.
他们不想让我们使用真正的NBC附属台，也就是WBRE。

1270
01:05:42.760 --> 01:05:46.780
But we had established WBRE in the show before.
但我们之前在节目里已经设定过WBRE了。

1271
01:05:47.540 --> 01:05:53.860
So, they had to get a signed clearance agreement from the real WBRE in Scranton.
所以，他们必须从斯克兰顿真正的WBRE那里获得一份签署的授权协议。

1272
01:05:54.560 --> 01:06:00.640
And eventually, we were given a pass so that we could use the actual call letters in the show.
最终，我们获得了许可，这样我们就可以在节目中使用真实的呼号了。

1273
01:06:01.350 --> 01:06:01.780
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1274
01:06:01.900 --> 01:06:03.960
And you can see it very clearly on the microphone.
而且你可以很清楚地在麦克风上看到它。

1275
01:06:04.220 --> 01:06:04.640
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1276
01:06:04.920 --> 01:06:05.360
Yeah.
是啊。

1277
01:06:05.360 --> 01:06:10.340
Well, this is going to set up a huge story arc now for Michael.
好吧，这现在要为迈克尔开启一个巨大的故事线了。

1278
01:06:10.940 --> 01:06:15.340
He's going to end up being the spokesperson for Saber.
他最终会成为赛博公司的代言人。

1279
01:06:15.900 --> 01:06:17.200
Joe is going to come back.
乔会回来的。

1280
01:06:17.400 --> 01:06:20.980
It's all going to go down next week in the whistleblower.
这一切都将在下周的《告密者》那一集中发生。

1281
01:06:21.880 --> 01:06:22.360
Yes.
是的。

1282
01:06:22.580 --> 01:06:25.780
The season finale whistleblower.
季终集《告密者》。

1283
01:06:26.600 --> 01:06:28.020
Well, that was the chump.
好吧，那真是个傻瓜。

1284
01:06:28.240 --> 01:06:29.660
Thank you for rewatching with us.
感谢你们与我们一起重温。

1285
01:06:29.820 --> 01:06:35.060
Thank you so much, Aaron Schur, for sending in those audio clips and sharing with us about writing this episode.
非常感谢亚伦·舒尔发来这些音频片段，并与我们分享撰写这一集的心得。

1286
01:06:35.360 --> 01:06:39.480
Thank you to Randy Cordray for always giving us awesome behind-the-scenes details.
感谢兰迪·科德雷总是为我们提供很棒的幕后细节。

1287
01:06:39.920 --> 01:06:44.380
And I would like to thank whoever put together that blooper reel on the Season 6 DVD.
我也想感谢制作第六季DVD花絮集锦的那个人。

1288
01:06:44.780 --> 01:06:48.140
Because, much like Trevor, I am finding it delightful.
因为，就像特雷弗一样，我觉得它非常有趣。

1289
01:06:49.220 --> 01:06:52.580
I would like to thank my engineer, Casey, here in New York.
我想感谢我在纽约的工程师凯西。

1290
01:06:52.820 --> 01:06:57.300
We did this podcast with me in New York and Angela in Los Angeles.
我们录制这期播客时，我在纽约，安吉拉在洛杉矶。

1291
01:06:57.960 --> 01:07:01.740
Casey and I might take off right now and get some of that lobster ice cream.
凯西和我现在可能要出发去尝尝那种龙虾冰淇淋了。

1292
01:07:01.740 --> 01:07:02.900
Okay.
好的。

1293
01:07:03.620 --> 01:07:05.100
We'll report back.
我们会回来汇报的。

1294
01:07:05.300 --> 01:07:06.620
We'll see you next week.
我们下周见。

1295
01:07:06.860 --> 01:07:08.120
We'll see you next time.
我们下次见。

1296
01:07:13.580 --> 01:07:15.420
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

